WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.380
In Great Britain, the richest
10 per cent of households

2
00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.660
held 43 per cent of all wealth.

3
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:10.280
The poorest half of households
held just 9 per cent.

4
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:13.680
Every country shares out its
income and wealth differently.

5
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.370
Some far more evenly than others.

6
00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.840
How can you sum up who
gets what in a whole

7
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.230
country with a single number?

8
00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:24.150
In this mission, you'll meet
the curve economists draw

9
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.420
to show how income is shared.

10
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.880
Then you'll use a graph lab to move income

11
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.260
between the richest and poorest fifths,

12
00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.020
and watch what happens.

13
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:36.140
Your mission: find out
how one number can sum

14
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.110
up who gets what in a country.
